{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookGNWRatio","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookGNWRatio","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookGNWWiring"],"declarations":26,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.gnwHookIdentity_proof","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.gnwHookIdentity_proof","kind":"theorem","line":449,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L449-L470","doc":"**(R4 / `gnwHookIdentity`) The GNW hook-summation identity, sorry-free.** Bridges the corner\nlist-sum to a `range` Finset sum (`filter_map_sum` + `list_range_sum`), replaces each term by the\nβ-Lagrange summand (corner: `gnw_corner_term`; non-corner: vanishes via `gnw_noncorner_vanish`), and\nevaluates via `betaLagrange_range = sz l`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.gnw_noncorner_vanish","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.gnw_noncorner_vanish","kind":"theorem","line":420,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L420-L447","doc":"**(R4) Non-corner rows vanish.** For `c < k` that is *not* a corner, the consecutive rows are equal\n(`l[c]=l[c+1]`), so `β_c − 1 = β_{c+1}` and the `j = c+1` numerator factor is `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.gnw_corner_term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.gnw_corner_term","kind":"theorem","line":409,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L409-L418","doc":"**(R4) The per-corner term in `range`/`betaNat` form.** For a corner `c`, the hook ratio equals the\nβ-Lagrange summand (R3 to drop the filter, R2 for the ratio, `prod_div_distrib` to split). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.filter_map_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.filter_map_sum","kind":"theorem","line":397,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L397-L407","doc":"List filter→map→sum equals the `if`-guarded map→sum over the whole list. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.list_range_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.list_range_sum","kind":"theorem","line":388,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L388-L395","doc":"`((List.range k).map g).sum = ∑ c ∈ Finset.range k, g c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaLagrange_range","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaLagrange_range","kind":"theorem","line":367,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L367-L386","doc":"**β-Lagrange in `range`/`betaNat` form, evaluating to `sz l`.** The `Fin`-indexed `betaLagrange`\nidentity reindexed to a `range` sum over the ℕ-valued `betaNat`, with the ratio split as\n(numerator product)/(denominator product = `vWeight`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prod_betaNat_erase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prod_betaNat_erase","kind":"theorem","line":347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L347-L365","doc":"Reindex a product over `univ.erase i` (Fin) as a product over `(range k).erase i.val` (ℕ),\nthrough `Fin.val`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prodHooks_removeCorner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prodHooks_removeCorner","kind":"theorem","line":335,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L335-L343","doc":"**(R3) `removeCorner` vs the `set`-decrement agree under `prodHooks`.** The only difference is the\ntrailing zero row dropped by the row-drop corner (`l[c]=1`); for a sorted shape that zero is a tail\nsuffix, invisible to `prodHooks`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prodHooks_filter_zero_sorted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prodHooks_filter_zero_sorted","kind":"theorem","line":306,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L306-L333","doc":"Filtering zeros out of a weakly-decreasing list leaves `prodHooks` unchanged: the zeros form a\ntail suffix, each removable by `prodHooks_append_zero`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prodHooks_append_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prodHooks_append_zero","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L280-L304","doc":"Appending a zero-length row leaves `prodHooks` unchanged: the new last row has empty inner\nproduct (factor `1`) and contributes to no other cell's leg (`colLen` unchanged). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.colLen_append_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.colLen_append_zero","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L273-L278","doc":"`colLen` ignores a trailing zero row (`0` is never `> j`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prodHooks_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prodHooks_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L238-L269","doc":"**(R2) The per-corner hook ratio (non-row-drop), sorry-free.** Combining the factorial side\n`betaFactProd_ratio` (= β_c) with the gap side `betaProdGap_ratio` through identity (i)\n`prodHooks·betaProdGap = betaFactProd` (`prodHooks_mul_betaProdGap`):\n`prodHooks(l)/prodHooks(l∖c) = β_c·∏_{j≠c}(β_c−1−β_j)/(β_c−β_j)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaFactProd_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaFactProd_pos","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L229-L236","doc":"`betaFactProd` is a positive natural number (product of factorials). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaProdGap_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaProdGap_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L202-L227","doc":"**(R1) The per-corner gap ratio (non-row-drop), sorry-free.** For a corner `c`,\n`betaProdGap (l.set c (l[c]−1)) = betaProdGap l · ∏_{j≠c}(β_c−1−β_j)/(β_c−β_j)`.  Factor each pairs\nterm `β'ᵢ−β'ⱼ = (βᵢ−βⱼ)·rᵢⱼ` (`mul_div_cancel₀`, gaps nonzero) and evaluate `∏ᵢ∏ⱼ rᵢⱼ` via\n`gap_ratio_prod`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.gap_ratio_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.gap_ratio_prod","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L122-L200","doc":"**The gap-ratio crux (R1 core).** The product of per-term ratios `(β'ᵢ−β'ⱼ)/(βᵢ−βⱼ)` over all\npairs `i<j<k` equals the GAP product `∏_{j≠c}(β_c−1−β_j)/(β_c−β_j)`.  Inner ratios are `1` off the\nindex-`c` factors (`hr1`); `i>c` columns vanish to `1`, `i<c` columns collapse to the single `j=c`\nfactor (sign-flipped to GAP shape), and the `i=c` column is GAP's `Ioo c k` part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaNat_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaNat_ne","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L117-L120","doc":"The gap factor `βᵢ − βⱼ` is nonzero for `i < j < k` (strict antitonicity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaNat_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaNat_lt","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L105-L115","doc":"`betaNat` is strictly antitone on indices `< length`: `i < j < k ⟹ βⱼ < βᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaProdGap_cast_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaProdGap_cast_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L98-L103","doc":"`betaProdGap` as a single product over the pairs `(i, j)` with `i < j < k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaNat_set_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaNat_set_self","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L91-L96","doc":"`betaNat (l.set c (l[c]−1))` at `c` is `betaNat l c − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaNat_set_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaNat_set_ne","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L86-L89","doc":"`betaNat (l.set c v)` agrees with `l` off `c` (cast of `betaNatVal_set_ne`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaNat_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaNat_eq","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L82-L84","doc":"`betaNat = betaNatVal` as a `ℚ` cast. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaProdGap_cast_pairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaProdGap_cast_pairs","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L73-L80","doc":"**`betaProdGap` as a pairs product** `∏_{i<j}(βᵢ−βⱼ)` organised by lower index `i` over `j ∈ (i,k)`.\nThis form isolates the index-`c` factors needed for the per-corner gap ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.row_range_eq_Ioo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.row_range_eq_Ioo","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L65-L71","doc":"The row-`i` gap factor as a product over the actual upper indices `j ∈ (i, k)`, dropping the\n`m ↦ i+1+m` reindex (`Finset.prod_Ico_eq_prod_range`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaFactProd_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaFactProd_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L40-L61","doc":"**Factorial side of the per-corner ratio (non-row-drop).** `betaFactProd l = β_c · betaFactProd(l∖c)`\nwith `l∖c = l.set c (l[c]−1)`: only factor `c` changes, contributing `β_c!/(β_c−1)! = β_c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaNatVal_set_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaNatVal_set_self","kind":"theorem","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L31-L38","doc":"`betaNatVal (l.set c (l[c]−1))` at `c` is `betaNatVal l c − 1` (needs the row positive). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaNatVal_set_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaNatVal_set_ne","kind":"theorem","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWRatio.lean#L23-L29","doc":"`betaNatVal (l.set c v)` agrees with `l` off index `c`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}